  // Hawkes Punch's space at REAL SCALE (SPACE-EPIC.md, J 2026-11-08: "make the planets actual planet size... think One Punch Man").
  // Two layers (Runtime/MVSpace.cs, AGENTS.md "Real-scale space"):
  //  - FAR: every "space" piece of kind body/ring/speck/crater is placed in KILOMETRES from the root (`space`), true radius, and drawn by the
  //    far layer (MV/SpaceFar), ray-traced along the near camera's own rays, so angular sizes and parallax are exact at any lens.
  //  - NEAR: the marks below are METRES from `origin`, as in every set: him, the double, effects, and the true-scale patches
  //    (ring ice `ring_field`, a moon's ground `moon_ground`, Jupiter's cloud deck `jupiter_deck`). A patch only shows while the focus is on its body.
  // The FOCUS says where the near world (the marks) is in the far one. Every card starts with one: {at: 0, do: focus, on: space_epic_space, name: <a focus below>}.
  // Up is up in each focus: on a surface the ground is y = 0; in the ring the ring plane is y = 0; "rot" tips the near world (rot [90,0,0] makes the planet a wall ahead, +z).
  // One hard sun from the far direction `sun`; MVSpace aims the near sun, a bounce from the brightest planet in view and a rim from behind him, per camera.
  "origin": [0, 0, 9000],
  "bounds": [-3000, -3000, 3000, 3000],
  "ceiling": 3000,
  "light": "space_epic",
